* TIMES.jl crafted case demo12_pfdf (reference/crafted.toml, 19 Nov 2026): demo12_pf (the
* REG1-REG2 power-flow grid, ELC the node of each region) plus a second grid node in REG1 (the
* line TU_ELC_TRA1 from ELC to TRAELC, as in demo12_pfd) and total demand fractions given as
* data, GR_DEMFR, with no sectoral fractions (no GR_ENDFR), so that powerflo.vda takes the total
* demand path GR_ENDC(R,NRG_GRID,'NRG') (L140) with nonzero fractions (M1.3 change 65), which no
* open model reaches:
* - L40-41: GR_DEMFR projected on (R,C) marks GR_GID, also for RSDELC, which is not a grid node;
* - L107: pp_lvlfc.mod levels GR_DEMFR to the DAYNITE timeslices of each node: an ANNUAL value
*   alone (ELC) is copied down; TRAELC has ANNUAL, the season W and the slice SD, so SD keeps its
*   own value, WD and WN take W's and SN inherits ANNUAL's; ELC is interpolated between 2005 and
*   2030 (fillparm, L194);
* - L131: every grid node gets its commodity timeslices in GR_DEMFR, EPS where there was none
*   (REG2's ELC), so EQ_GR_DEMALL rows exist there too;
* - L149-154 normalise the REG1 fractions over the two nodes; L155-162 pick the reference node.
$ONEMPTY
$ONEPS
$ONWARNING
SET PRC
/
TU_ELC_TRA1
/

SET PRC_MAP
/
REG1.IRE.TU_ELC_TRA1
/

SET PRC_TSL
/
REG1.TU_ELC_TRA1.DAYNITE
/

SET PRC_ACTUNT
/
REG1.TU_ELC_TRA1.NRG.PJ
/

SET TOP_IRE
/
 REG1.ELC.REG1.TRAELC.TU_ELC_TRA1
/

SET PRC_DESC
/
 REG1.TU_ELC_TRA1 'Crafted: line from ELC to the transport electricity node (TIMES.jl demo12_pfdf)'
/

PARAMETER PRC_REACT /
REG1.2005.TU_ELC_TRA1 0.1
/;

PARAMETER GR_DEMFR /
REG1.2005.ELC.ANNUAL 0.7
REG1.2030.ELC.ANNUAL 0.6
REG1.2005.TRAELC.ANNUAL 0.3
REG1.2005.TRAELC.W 0.4
REG1.2005.TRAELC.SD 0.25
REG1.2005.RSDELC.ANNUAL 0.5
/;
